-even-rounding-0a9452f727"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 748865, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016CauYUcfDD1caStUTtG6XZ", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding-0a9452f727", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 748865, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016CauYUcfDD1caStUTtG6XZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 753984, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** The first run (ci-0001) passed, but the PR couldn't be opened because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, checked that the fix was still there, and CI (ci-0002) passed again on the updated branch.\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't read it myself. I went by the code's docstring and the test, which both ask for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LVeGhkNJu5MdC1kx1nc93d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QMKgrMBPqK3wMEzAvrVJEN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file"